    "Fin.lt_def aligns only the existing Fin value comparison with its already split predicate. The three new testBit facts are the closed false bits1,2,3 of the unchanged singleton mask1; each is delegated to kernel decide in the candidate, not accepted from an external checker.",
    "Rewrite the existing singleton selected-mass identity before unfolding its Fin constructor; the backward four-full-square direction uses the same four existing conjunction components with only additive association normalization.",
    "Continuity and measurability transport the same cap, selected-square, cap-prefix residual and zero functions. Explicit Set.ofPred_forall identifies only the original outer Fin4 forall with its intersection; selected and unselected implication sets are respectively univ and the original strict inequality set.",
    "The original full eligibility supplies residual greater than the actual smallest coordinate. The actual H248(max2,...) range gives the original 0..20000/417 bound, without strengthening to residual>=2w or adding a table-bound hypothesis.",
    "Both accepted-target headers and the integrability application use exactly Part5UpperTables.H248. Part5UpperTables.measurable_H248 is the existing literal-table measurability supplier. Consumer KnotPayment already opens that table namespace; Oscillation already spells the same FQN. No downstream source was changed."
  ],
